What each one does, simply:

forgot-password/page.tsx — a page with an email box. When submitted, it always shows "check your email," whether or not that email exists. This stops attackers from guessing valid emails.
request-password-reset.ts — checks the email, checks the rate limit (3 tries per hour per email), asks Supabase to send the reset link. Never reveals if the email was found.
reset-password.ts — where the person picks a new password after clicking the emailed link. Checks the password is strong enough and matches the confirm box, then saves it.
reset-password/page.tsx — the page with the new password form, shown after clicking the emailed link.
rate-limit.ts — the shared rate limit rules, so both login and password reset use the same setup.
